          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Straightforward checking on
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
          %h3#Properties Properties
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a microlinear space.
          %p
            %strong Sketch of Proposition
          %p We want to show that the morphism of simplicial sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Delta^{op},\mathcal{T}](U \times D, X^{(\Delta_\inf^\bullet)})
                  \\to
                  [\Delta^{op},\mathcal{T}](U , X^{(\Delta_\inf^\bullet)})
          %p
            induced by pullback along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \simeq U \times * \to U \times D
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          %p
            %strong Sketch of proof
          %p
            First consider the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            itself has no infinitesimal directions in that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(U,D) = *
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Delta^{op},\mathcal{T}](U \times D, X^{(\Delta_\inf^\bullet)})
                  \\to
                  [\Delta^{op},\mathcal{T}](U , X^{(\Delta_\inf^\bullet)})
            is an acyclic Kan fibration in that all squares
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi 𝒯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo ×
                          %mi D
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi Δ
                                %mi inf
                                %mo •
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi 𝒯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi Δ
                                %mi inf
                                %mo •
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\partial \Delta[n] &amp;\to&amp; [\Delta^{op},\mathcal{T}](U \times D, X^{(\Delta_\inf^\bullet)})
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Delta[n]
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  [\Delta^{op},\mathcal{T}](U , X^{(\Delta_\inf^\bullet)})
                  }
          %p have lifts.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
            this says that the map is surjective on vertices, which it is, since any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
            is in the image of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times D \to U \times * \simeq U \to X
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            we need to check that every homotopy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi D
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X^D \times D
            downstairs with fixed lifts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times D \to X
            over the endpoints may be lifted. But by assumption
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to D
            factors through the point, so that the homotopy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi D
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X^D \times D \stackrel{\to}{\to} X
            has the same source as target
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : U \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi ϵ
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (u,\epsilon) \mapsto (f(u) + \epsilon \nu_i(u)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=1,2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_i
            tangent vectors. A homotopy between these is given by a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi D
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times D \to X^D \times D
            defined by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi ν
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi ν
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (u,\epsilon) \mapsto (f(u)+ (-)\nu_1(u) + (\epsilon-(-))\nu_2(u), \epsilon)
          %p
            Finally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            we have unique flllers, because by construction every morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]\cdot Y \to X^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})}
            is uniquely fixed by the restriction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta[n] \to \Delta[n]\cdot Y \to X^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})}
            to its boundary.
          %p
            The case for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times D
            replaced with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times D^n
            works analogously.
